  "subject": "two adults in their thirties retaking the DSE at a Mong Kok evening school who share her calculator all term because his battery is dead, though she has seen the unopened pack of new batteries in his bag, and who open their results envelopes together on the school steps",
  "caption": "Cantonese country-pop with a Nashville front-porch feel. A strummed steel-string acoustic guitar, a pedal steel sliding under every line, a fiddle answering the vocal in the gaps, a light five-string banjo roll in the chorus, round electric bass, a brushed snare with a soft kick. Clean, warm, sunlit studio mix, instruments close and dry with a little room air. A warm female mid-range lead, plain and conversational, a light crack on the long notes, a soft male harmony joining on the last chorus. 100 BPM, A major. Shy, sunny and hopeful. No trap beat, no autotune, no EDM drop, no rap section, no Cantopop piano ballad, no stadium rock guitars.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n旺角夜校 逢星期二四\n三十幾歲人 返嚟再考文憑試\n隔籬個男人 部計數機開極都開唔着\n佢話冇電 塊面紅到耳仔\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我將我部 推去兩張枱中間\n你一題 我一題 輪住㩒\n\n[Chorus]\n一部計數機 兩個人\n你㩒完 推返過嚟我呢邊\n啲掣仲暖 你啱啱㩒過\n成晚 我條數都計唔啱\n\n[Verse]\n開學冇幾耐 佢個書包跌落地\n跌咗排新電芯出嚟 未拆過\n佢執返入去 扮冇事\n照樣問我 部計數機借唔借\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我冇出聲 照樣推過去\n兩個人 擰轉面偷笑\n\n[Chorus]\n一部計數機 兩個人\n你㩒完 推返過嚟我呢邊\n你書包嗰排電芯 我唔講\n等你 一直借到最後一堂\n\n[Bridge]\n七月放榜嗰朝 學校門口\n揸住信封 坐喺石級上面\n佢話 數到三 一齊拆\n\n[Chorus]\n兩個信封 兩個人\n你合格 我都合格\n部計數機 你終於還返畀我\n你話 下次想借我隻手\n\n[Outro]\n借畀你 唔使還",
